1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,260
Listen to a talk on a podcast about psychology.

2
00:00:03,260 --> 00:00:07,320
Podcast Host: Did you see that new thriller movie that came out last week

3
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:09,180
I did and loved it.

4
00:00:09,180 --> 00:00:12,932
The action, the plot twists... I was totally captivated.

5
00:00:12,932 --> 00:00:20,020
Time just flew by. Not a single thought occurred to me that was unrelated to the movie.

6
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:25,099
What I experienced is what psychologists call hard fascination.

7
00:00:25,099 --> 00:00:29,050
Hard fascination means intense focus and concentration.

8
00:00:29,050 --> 00:00:32,600
Whether it's TV programs, video games

9
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:37,040
hard fascination is all too easy to come by in this modern world.

10
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:41,260
There's another type of fascination-soft fascination.

11
00:00:41,260 --> 00:00:44,400
There's still effortless attention

12
00:00:44,420 --> 00:00:47,326
meaning that no special effort is required for you to stay focused,

13
00:00:47,326 --> 00:00:50,180
but there's still room for other thoughts.

14
00:00:50,180 --> 00:00:54,486
When I take a walk in the park and look at the flowers and trees,

15
00:00:54,486 --> 00:00:59,080
for example, I might be thinking in the back of my mind about my dinner plans.

16
00:00:59,080 --> 00:01:04,210
Now, one thing to know is hard fascination causes mental fatigue.

17
00:01:04,210 --> 00:01:09,060
The mind is so intensely focused that it gets tired fast.

18
00:01:09,060 --> 00:01:16,020
What follows mental fatigue? You might find yourself easily distracted, irritable, and stressed.

19
00:01:16,020 --> 00:01:22,570
Soft fascination, in contrast, engages a different part of the brain. The DMN,

20
00:01:22,570 --> 00:01:29,120
or Default Mode Network, which soothes the mind and helps combat mental fatigue.

21
00:01:29,120 --> 00:01:32,480
So next time you feel like your mind is on overload

22
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:36,017
turn off the TV, put down your phone.

23
00:01:36,017 --> 00:01:40,010
Take a walk, or simply sit and stare at the clouds.
